      <location value="309"/>
      Fig. S12 | Performance comparison on cpg0000.
    </caption>
    <description>
      <content>SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE

Single scatter plot titled “Well level-Compounds.” The x-axis is labeled “Mean Average Precision (mAP)” with ticks from about 0.1 to 0.4. The y-axis is labeled “Folds of Enrichment” with ticks around 15, 20, 30, and 40.

Visible data: four colored circular markers with black outlines:
- Blue point near mAP 0.13, enrichment 15
- Orange point near mAP 0.16, enrichment 19
- Green point near mAP 0.22, enrichment 24
- Red point near mAP 0.36, enrichment 39

No visible panel letters, legend, biological source objects, microscopy images, molecular structures, transformations, or model architecture/interface diagrams are shown. The figure suggests a positive relationship between mAP and folds of enrichment across four compound-level/well-level conditions, with the red point performing highest on both metrics.</content>
    </description>
  </picture>
